  "description": "CR 717.2b a Class retains its level even if it stops being a Class",
  "note": "Song of the Dryads makes the Class a Forest land: Land replaces Enchantment, and the Class subtype goes with the type it correlates with (CR 205.1a). Its land-subtype change also strips the permanent's abilities (CR 305.7), so while the Song is on it the Piker is 2/1 for that reason and not for a lost level. The Class is levelled to 2 before the Song arrives, so the readings differ once Disenchant takes the Song away: a level discarded while it was not a Class would leave it at CR 717.2d's default of 1, the Piker 2/1 and the level-2 bar offered; it is 3/2 and the bar is refused. The Haskell test moved the Song onto a Mountain rather than destroying it.",
